From: Beam Engineering <support@beam.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH] Reject pending vhost-user block requests before snapshotting

QSD 8.2 does not save inflight requests. A memory snapshot taken before
its block requests complete can restore a guest with permanently lost
writeback completions. Require every vhost-user block queue to be empty
before capturing any device, including destructive virtiofs state.

Return 429 only for the typed preflight failure, leaving the original VM
resumable so callers can thaw and retry. Other snapshot failures retain
their existing status and lifecycle semantics.

Applies to Cloud Hypervisor v53.0, commit
9ed824d6d08df3e96f7d5f50795d9449ac99f431.

